Verilator metasim: lint_off WIDTHEXPAND/UNSIGNED.

Saturn and Gemmini RTL trips these warnings, which the metasim build treats as
errors. Generic, though upstream may prefer narrower waivers.

diff --git a/sim/midas/src/main/cc/rtlsim/ml-verilator-conf.vlt b/sim/midas/src/main/cc/rtlsim/ml-verilator-conf.vlt
index 1e240378429713ef2ae7c2e142f5623570936717..9a858b026e389f9e62e6d4de3cf56b60a6610517 100644
--- a/sim/midas/src/main/cc/rtlsim/ml-verilator-conf.vlt
+++ b/sim/midas/src/main/cc/rtlsim/ml-verilator-conf.vlt
@@ -3,3 +3,12 @@
 // driven by separate ports.
 `verilator_config
 lint_off -rule MULTIDRIVEN
+
+// Metasimulating the RiskyBird Saturn+Gemmini target trips three lint warnings
+// in generated RTL which -Wall promotes to fatal errors, so the build cannot
+// even start. Neither is a real defect: a DIV whose RHS constant is narrower
+// than the expression, and two comparisons that are constant under unsigned
+// arithmetic. Suppressed by rule rather than with -Wno-fatal so genuine
+// warnings still fail the build.
+lint_off -rule WIDTHEXPAND
+lint_off -rule UNSIGNED
